# config.py reads everything from .env/environment variables — it holds
# no secrets itself — but per request it's ignored here too. Practical
# effect: future code changes to config.py won't come through on
# `git pull` on the server; they'll need to be applied manually each
# time. If that becomes annoying, the alternative is un-ignoring it
# (safe, since it has no secrets) and relying on .env alone for anything
# sensitive.
config.py

# Local database — back this up separately, don't rely on git for it.
hospital.db
